00:29:07.569 --> 00:29:14.376
From Real Python: LangChain Tutorial: From Prompts to RAG and AI Agents.

00:29:14.481 --> 00:29:19.967
LangChain is a framework for Python and JavaScript that lets you build applications powered

00:29:19.967 --> 00:29:26.278
by large language models (LLMs). Sending a single prompt to a model takes only

00:29:26.278 --> 00:29:33.334
a couple of lines of code. However, real apps also need reusable instructions, access

00:29:33.334 --> 00:29:36.931
to your own data, and a way for the model to call your Python

00:29:36.931 --> 00:29:44.917
code. In this tutorial, you’ll explore how LangChain’s Python library handles each of these.

00:29:44.917 --> 00:29:49.945
Say a group of hospitals just handed you a spreadsheet full of patient reviews,

00:29:49.945 --> 00:29:55.723
together with a short request: Find out what patients are saying about us. You

00:29:55.723 --> 00:29:59.945
could read through every row yourself, but by the time you’re done, the next

00:29:59.945 --> 00:30:03.456
batch of reviews will probably have arrived.

